Z||000000||jaguiler||03-29-2001||09:55 PM||||Hello All,<P>I have searched and searched and have not seen anyone with this problem.  I have a manifold leak on the rear manifold.  I have identified the location:<P>"Another place to check would be the coupling, where the exhaust system connects to the headpipe. (It's the big coupling, just in front of the transmission.)"<P>This joint is just under and in back (closer to trnk) of the throttle body sensor.  Also just above and to the left of number five spark plug. I have a 2.8 V6.  <P>Problem -  I have looks at this joint and it looks like my manifold has a small notch cut into the place where it fits in the Y poipe or headpipe.  I guess I could tighten the flange...but is there anything I could use to seal this small notch?  Some chemical... I would rather not go to a welder... is there another option... I was thinking of separating the joint and sanding both urfaces so they join better... is there a donut washer that can go there? Sory for long post....I'm just getting tired of the tick tick sound....<P><P>------------------<BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||65.8.46.102||reg||8
Z||000001||tgowens||03-30-2001||01:31 AM||||yes, there is a donut -- replace it if you separate the pipes.........||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||03-30-2001||04:38 AM||||I think that he is talking about the manifold coupling to the crossover pipe. Not the crossover pipe to the rest of the exhaust. There is no magic "goop" to seal the coupling so unbolt it and readjust it. If the mounts are bad sometimes the engine movement shifts the coupling. Thats all. I did that to mine and haven't had a problem since. Mine had that notch too but it doesn't leak. Not sure what its for...<P>If it doesn't seal check it closly for cracks!<P>Hope this helps!<p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 03-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||jaguiler||03-30-2001||07:48 AM||||great I'll give tightening it a try....i hope it works!! If not I will unbolt the pieses and sand both sides while it is still on the a car and then try rejoining.<BR>thanks<P><P>------------------<BR>______<BR>__|aguiler||65.8.46.102||reg||1
